im revolt of 1864 the Dungans and Taranchis of the Ili valley set up the Taranchi Sultanate; Russia occupied Ili in 1871 and returned most of it to China by the Treaty of Saint Petersburg (1881). Yettishar did not hold Ili.","uncertain":"From general knowledge, not checked against the sources: the Muslim Chagatai khans at Almaliq in the 14th century; Tacheng and the Altai were probably never under a Muslim state at all, so for them “influence only” may be the truer shade.","sources":[{"t":"Ili Kazakh Autonomous Prefecture (Wikipedia)","u":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ili_Kazakh_Autonomous_Prefecture","k":"modern","s":"the Taranchi Sultanate formed by Dungans and Taranchis in the Muslim revolt of 1864; part returned to China by the Treaty of Saint Petersburg, 1881"},{"t":"Russia’s withdrawal from the Ili valley in 1881 (The Cartographer)","u":"https://cartographer.substack.com/p/russias-withdrawal-from-the-ili-river","k":"modern","s":"Russian occupation of Ili from 1871"}],"km2":351844,"c":[-94.461,-45.377],"polys":[[[[79.85,41.376],[79.9,41.326],[79.9,41.276],[79.926,41.25],[80.224,41.25],[80.276,41.3],[80.376,41.3],[80.4,41.326],[80.4,41.376],[80.426,41.4],[80.776,41.4],[80.8,41.424],[80.826,41.45],[80.85,41.476],[80.85,42.126],[80.826,42.15],[80.956,42.166],[81.116,42.184],[81.278,42.202],[81.37,42.152],[81.46,42.102],[81.552,42.05],[81.712,42.068],[81.874,42.086],[82.036,42.104],[82.196,42.12],[82.358,42.138],[82.43,42.206],[82.59,42.22],[82.752,42.238],[82.914,42.254],[82.986,42.322],[83.012,42.416],[82.994,42.534],[82.974,42.656],[83.002,42.75],[83.164,42.766],[83.49,42.796],[83.564,42.862],[83.726,42.878],[83.89,42.892],[84.054,42.906],[84.218,42.918],[84.38,42.932],[84.47,42.88],[84.634,42.892],[84.752,42.932],[84.782,43.026],[84.856,43.092],[85.184,43.116],[85.346,43.128],[85.474,43.106],[85.6,43.086],[85.764,43.096],[85.884,43.134],[85.87,43.256],[85.858,43.376],[85.888,43.468],[85.964,43.534],[86.04,43.598],[86.162,43.638],[86.148,43.758],[86.224,43.822]